//! EGL / GLES extension entry points as exported symbols, for AOSP code built against the host's GL loaders (providers.toml rows `libEGL`, `libGLESv1_CM`, `libGLESv2`, `libGLESv3`).
//! AOSP's libEGL exports every extension function it knows; the host's (libglvnd) exports only the core API and hands out extensions through `eglGetProcAddress`, so AOSP code calling `eglCreateImageKHR`, `glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES`, ... directly links against nothing.
//! Here each extension function of AOSP's pinned Khronos headers is a shell (generated by build.rs) that looks its implementation up with `eglGetProcAddress` on first call and forwards to it, arguments and result unchanged.
//! The lookup is per process: EGL 1.5 §3.10 makes the returned pointers context-independent, valid for every display and context.
//! Linked next to the host library, never in its place; it defines no core function, so lookups of the host's own symbols are unaffected.
//!
//! Boundary crate: `unsafe` only in `ffi`.
#![deny(unsafe_code)]

#[allow(unsafe_code)]
mod ffi;
